  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Peraton Enterprise Solutions obligated $600M in federal contracts in FY2026 to date. Peraton Enterprise Solutions won 90 awards so far this fiscal year, with an average award size of $6.7M, and obligations are down 38.8% year over year. Historical obligations show FY25 at $980M, FY24 at $1.1B, FY23 at $1.1B, FY22 at $967M, and FY21 at $1.4B. The General Services Administration provided the largest share of FY2026 obligations at $179M, followed by the Department of Defense at $116M and the Department of the Treasury at $75.9M. Computer Systems Design Services is the largest market for Peraton Enterprise Solutions at $468M, with Electronic Computer Manufacturing at $75.9M and Other Computer Related Services at $32.7M. Current-year totals are partial and cover fiscal year to date, so FY2026 figures reflect activity through the reporting period rather than a full fiscal year total.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How big is Peraton Enterprise Solutions' federal business in FY2026 to date?",
        "body": "Peraton Enterprise Solutions obligated $600M in FY2026 to date. Peraton Enterprise Solutions won 90 awards with an average award size of $6.7M, and obligations are down 38.8% year over year. Recent fiscal-year comparisons include FY25 at $980M and FY24 at $1.1B, showing higher totals in prior years."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies and markets account for Peraton Enterprise Solutions' obligations?",
        "body": "Peraton Enterprise Solutions received the largest agency obligations from the General Services Administration at $179M and the Department of Defense at $116M. Peraton Enterprise Solutions' top markets are Computer Systems Design Services at $468M, Electronic Computer Manufacturing at $75.9M, and Other Computer Related Services at $32.7M."
      }
    ]
